title The scope that changed between rows
prompt THE BATON -- Patchouli's lane is mantra/ and tally/; the charter names a weave Mantra has yet to grow.
think Opened with fleet_round_open (already on the anointed order at 88721dde7f), read the card whole, and took the rota row from git rev-list --count HEAD = 3985, so 3985 mod 5 = 0 -- the Aether row, why the work exists. An aether lap listens for the page nobody answered.
think Reds first before any new work. Three rows stand on the pin: %438 CLOSED, %431 OPEN at custody gate %1, %360 OPEN with its remainder explicitly in other lanes. Neither open row is mine to close, so both are surfaced rather than routed around, and my lane's own queue was not empty.
think My lane's next movement was the charter's "The line, and its count" -- three rounds to write one Rye module holding a line, its arrival, its departure, and the integer that ticks between them. Before naming a new module I swept the tree for `weave` collisions, which references-are-promises asks for. The sweep returned mantra/src/weave.rye.
think Measured rather than concluded. The charter's table reads `mantra/` Rye modules 32 and lines 9,175; flat `mantra/*.rye` is 27 and 7,976. So rows one and two are recursive and the row the conclusion rests on -- ``mantra/*.rye`` mentioning conflict, merge, three-way or diff3, 0 -- is flat. Run recursively that grep reads 1, and it names mantra/src/weave.rye. The 1,199-line difference is exactly mantra/src/.
think Checked whether the file is live tissue or a fossil before booking anything. It has stood since the root commit 7d991702f; four rostered guards at tier lap read it by name; rye/tests/mantra_weave_test.rye exercises it; mantra/src/main.rye is a working CLI whose own header states the weave the charter says is unbuilt.
think Then read the two commits and found they are one. b4a647f68 rostered mantra_gen_floor_a1_gate and glow_tend_limb1 through limb3 AND added the essay saying the weave waits to be built. The commit turned on the proofs of the thing it declared missing.
think Chose the repair by tier. The essay is dated testimony, so facts go by erratum and every word above it stands. tools/l/patchouli_seat_prompt.txt is a living path with no stamp in its basename, so it corrects in place -- and it is TRACKED, which is why the claim was reaching every launch of this ship.
think Judged the class worth a loom rather than a note. Measured the flat-glob blind spot tree-wide: 14 of 44 rooms, 513 files. The same lantern has fired twice before from the other side -- room_bound's dated pattern read ZERO for tools/ for that room's whole life, and %175's sprig pattern read 237 logs as living.
obs THE CHARTER IS NOT WRONG ABOUT ANY NUMBER. Every figure in its six-row table is correct and row six labels its own glob honestly. What crossed the two scopes is the CONCLUSION, which reads six rows under one heading as one measurement. That is a fairer and sharper statement than "the measurement was wrong," and it is the one the row makes.
obs MY OWN GATE WAS ONE SUBTRACTION FROM DECORATIVE. I first computed hidden as recursive - flat, which makes the check flat + hidden == recursive true for every input -- a gate that cannot red, in a guard written to enforce that very law. Writing the control's mutation leg is what exposed it. hidden is counted by its own pattern now, and the control breaks one pattern in a copy and proves the refusal fires.
obs The essay's crux survives intact and I said so plainly. Merge, conflict-showing and order-independence genuinely do not exist; the word merge appears in weave.rye exactly once, in a comment on current() anticipating it. What moves is where the arc STARTS: movement two built, movement three half built, the next real work is merge rather than Line.
obs Both reds on the cold pass are known and neither is new. commit_message_guard is %431 verbatim -- SEED_PUBLISHER_ARMS 0, ten of eleven readings green, GUARD_OK. agent_jail answers bwrap: Failed to make / slave: Operation not permitted with four legs passing, which is bwrap refusing to nest inside this session's own sandbox: an environment fact, and literally the card's own reflex about a guard that cannot run its instrument saying which instrument.
obs mantra/README.md line 36 names src/weave.rye outright. The information was one file away in the room's own front door, which is why the repair reaches the measurement habit rather than the room's documentation.
obs mantra/src/weave.rye still carries two non-ASCII characters in comments after a commit titled "comments swept to plain ASCII" -- a double arrow at line 24 and an arrow at line 73. Named here rather than swept, because this lap's keystone is the red and the ratchet turns on touch by the lap that opens that file.
